   </property>
   <widget class="QWidget" name="tab_histogram">
    <attribute name="title">
     <string>Histogram</string>
    </attribute>
    <widget class="QGraphicsView" name="graphicsView_hystogram">
     <property name="geometry">
      <rect>
       <x>10</x>
       <y>20</y>
       <width>441</width>
       <height>341</height>
      </rect>
     </property>
     <property name="frameShape">
      <enum>QFrame::Shape::Box</enum>
     </property>
     <property name="verticalScrollBarPolicy">
      <enum>Qt::ScrollBarPolicy::ScrollBarAlwaysOff</enum>
     </property>
     <property name="horizontalScrollBarPolicy">
      <enum>Qt::ScrollBarPolicy::ScrollBarAlwaysOff</enum>
     </property>
     <property name="sizeAdjustPolicy">
      <enum>QAbstractScrollArea::SizeAdjustPolicy::AdjustToContents</enum>
     </property>
    </widget>
   </widget>
   <widget class="QWidget" name="tab_info">
    <attribute name="title">
     <string>Info</string>
    </attribute>
    <widget class="QTextEdit" name="textEdit">
     <property name="geometry">
      <rect>
       <x>10</x>
       <y>10</y>
       <width>441</width>
       <height>341</height>
      </rect>
     </property>
     <property name="readOnly">
      <bool>true</bool>
     </property>
     <property name="html">
      <string>&lt;!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC &quot;-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0//EN&quot; &quot;http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/strict.dtd&quot;&gt;
&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta name=&quot;qrichtext&quot; content=&quot;1&quot; /&gt;&lt;meta charset=&quot;utf-8&quot; /&gt;&lt;style type=&quot;text/css&quot;&gt;
p, li { white-space: pre-wrap; }
hr { height: 1px; border-width: 0; }
li.unchecked::marker { content: &quot;\2610&quot;; }
li.checked::marker { content: &quot;\2612&quot;; }
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body style=&quot; font-family:'Segoe UI'; font-size:9pt; font-weight:400; font-style:normal;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;Quick Summary&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;The plugin allows you to classify raster values into custom intervals and generate a new reclassified raster based on the values defined in the table. You can select the input raster and band, customize histogram and line colors, and choose among several classification methods: &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;Equal Interval&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;Quantile&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;K‑means&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;Natural Breaks (approx.)&lt;/span&gt;, and &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;User&lt;/span&gt;. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;In &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;User mode&lt;/span&gt;, intervals can be defined in two ways: &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; margin-right: 0px; -qt-list-indent: 1;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;Manually&lt;/span&gt;, by typing interval limits and new class values directly into the table. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;Interactively&lt;/span&gt;, by selecting a table row and clicking on the histogram.&lt;br /&gt;The plugin automatically fills the interval boundaries according to the selected row: &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; margin-right: 0px; -qt-list-indent: 1;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;First row:&lt;/span&gt; Start = raster minimum, End = clicked value &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;Intermediate rows:&lt;/span&gt; Start = previous row’s End, End = clicked value &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;Penultimate row:&lt;/span&gt; Same as intermediate rows, and the &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;last row is filled automatically&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;Last row:&lt;/span&gt; Start = previous End, End = raster maximum &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;Each click draws a vertical line on the histogram. Only &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;one movable line&lt;/span&gt; is kept per row, while &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;fixed boundary lines&lt;/span&gt; (minimum or maximum) are drawn automatically for the first and last intervals. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;The table displays interval limits, new class values, and raster statistics (count, min, max, mean, standard deviation). Interval values can be exported to CSV/TXT, and in User mode the table can also be filled by importing a CSV/TXT file with three columns. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;The &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;Output Raster&lt;/span&gt; section lets you choose where to save the reclassified raster and optionally load it into QGIS. Additional actions include running the classification, resetting the session, saving the table, exporting the histogram, and closing the plugin. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
     </property>
    </widget>
   </widget>
  </widget>
